{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/952374-data-as-a-mind","id":952374,"title":"Data as a Mind?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-17T00:36:26-07:00","id":952374,"title":"Data as a Mind?","content":"Hey guys. I wanted to bounce an idea off of you all to see if it made sense mechanically and wasn't unbalancing.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, some part of it came from Ascension, but there is some small bit that can be found in the Arcana descriptions of Mind, and I feel like it makes more sense in Awakening, and would probably take some stretching and a go-ahead from a ST for use in Ascension. I'll also admit that I haven't read all of the Awakening supplements, so if this has been addressed, go ahead a stop me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for the sake of the Mind Arcana, what do you think about using Mind spells to affect computers? Reading, decoding/encoding, damaging even? It seems to me that computers are rough approximations of minds, although simple and limited in scope and complexity. Once could even go so far as to say that their Supernal ideals would in fact be simple Minds. Since a Master of Mind can in fact create a new Mind ex nihilo, it seems to me that they're not limited to natural creatures/spirits, and artificial minds might fall into the Aracana's purvue. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:59:04-07:00","id":952378,"title":"","content":"First off, I don't think there's a case to be made that software has reached the point to call a &quot;mind.&quot; AI could happen, and Mind should be able to interact with an AI as a Mind, but that's not where computers are.<br /> <br /> Second, the computer itself wouldn't be the &quot;mind,&quot; any more than a brain would be. While Life and Mind can overlap when it comes to this stuff, if you want to mess with the physical &quot;meat&quot; you use Life. Screwing with a computer is going to be Matter or Forces depending on what you're trying to manipulate. Forces doesn't even need anything else to &quot;understand&quot; wireless transmissions at Forces 1. You can listen in on a cell phone conversation by just watching the phone and seeing the data transmissions directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:07:56-07:00","id":952381,"title":"","content":"It's a tough question, historically the game hasn't been all that clear on where Data fits into spheres/arcana. It's changed from edition to edition. A lot of 1st Edition Mage: The Awakening spells treated data/information as covered by the mind arcanum. 2nd Edition or Chronicles hasn't had much yet on it, which makes it hard to decide how it should fit in with the rules. <br /> <br /> I would say that computers themselves aren't Mind, just like a Mastigos can't go around summoning brains out of thin out with Mind (that would require Life) they likewise couldn't summon computers (that would require Matter). However the data stored on those computers? I think that's a much more likely target for Mind magic.<br /> <br /> For example in my opinion a Mind Fraying could never damage the physical circuitry of a computer. However corrupting and erasing the data stored on it? That's a lot more likely, though I'd say it comes down to your storyteller's interpretation. I'm still not sure exactly what my position would be on it in 2nd Edition. I haven't fully wrapped my head around the new edition's stance on Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:17:44-07:00","id":952384,"title":"","content":"Data on electronics falls under Forces until such time as programs become complex enough to form AI. I'm pretty sure it was that way in 1e as well. Data found in the mind falls under Mind, is that what you were thinking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-17-2016, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:31:58-07:00","id":952386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/952374-data-as-a-mind?p=952384#post952384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Data on electronics falls under Forces until such time as programs become complex enough to form AI. I'm pretty sure it was that way in 1e as well. Data found in the mind falls under Mind, is that what you were thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, I'm very confused. I have clear and distinct memories of 1st Edition rotes that combined Matter + Mind to handle information written on a book but I've quickly flipped through every 1st Edition book I can lay my hands on and can't find it. I'm not sure anymore.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Nope, sorry, can't find a single word on it anywhere. I must have mistaken a house rule for something cannon or something. Not sure. Sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":". 08-17-2016, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T02:17:22-07:00","id":952397,"title":"","content":"Also, 2e has some very clear examples in things like Tune In (Forces 1, p. 141), and Transmission (Forces 2, p. 144) that Forces covers working directly with data while it's in the form of energy. Matter or Forces can both let you operate a computer at range (Matter would use Remote Control with a Reach option, Forces would need TK to operate the keys and such, for something a bit easier than trying to manipulate code directly via electric manipulation). The only potentially useful Mind effect in this is Universal Language, since it lets you break encryption, which the Forces spells seem to indicate they don't do automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T02:19:06-07:00","id":952399,"title":"","content":"I found what I was thinking of. The spell Living Library from page 22 of Sanctum and Sigil but I was mis-remembering it slightly. It uses mind not for the information, but in order to copy it into a living being's mind. <br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T02:54:48-07:00","id":952405,"title":"","content":"I'm not really suggesting affecting a computer physically, although I suppose the ramifications of electronic information storing <i>would</i> sort of require the electronics to reflect the state of stored data. Reading wouldn't alter any state, but I suppose writing, encrypting/decrypting, and creating/destroying stored data would.<br /> <br /> Really what I was getting at is the distinction between man and beast being a similar distinction between a full conscious and self-aware mind and a simpler, simulated mind, which is arguably what a computer is. Supernally speaking, what is a computer's perfected state? If one can use Life to influence and then control beasts (and up to people), beasts being simpler life forms and thus easier to affect, then the same could be true for simpler minds, right? Is it possible that all we need to do is interpret the data and programming on a computer as an artificial mind, albeit lacking in true self-awareness (like lesser animals and insects), and then it could fall under the influence of the Mind Arcana?<br /> <br /> Also yes, Forces is explicitly how a mage can &quot;read&quot; electronic transmissions and stored data, but when it comes to Mage, there's more than one Arcana to skin a cat, yes?<br /> <br /> Not to be stubborn about this, just trying to more clearly state my case. Again, I'm a bit of an Awakening amateur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T03:38:19-07:00","id":952410,"title":"","content":"In 2e they don't make the distinction between animal and human so clear cut, it's just as easy or difficult to affect one as the other. What's less clear and would better support your position as a corollary is if animals are still considered to have minds in 2e. Off the top of my head (Feel free to correct me) I don't recall seeing any of the Mind spells mention that they can be used on animals.<br /> <br /> That said, there are some things Mind can for sure do for you, for instance it can ramp up your Computer skill, or translate binary code and programming languages for you. Which means you could write code as well with a natural touch beyond what most can accomplish. Just write data mining software.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-17-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:02:50-07:00","id":952692,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it, but I'd require taking a Reach for it to work at all, and possibly make them spend a Mana point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}